---
import V3Layout from '../../../layouts/v3/V3Layout.astro';
import visitsData from '../../../data/curated-visits.json';
import { workBySlug } from '../../../lib/catalog';
import { shortWorkTitle } from '../../../lib/work-titles';
import { withBase } from '../../../lib/urls';

const editions = Object.entries(visitsData.visits);
---

<V3Layout title="How we curate" description="The selection, sources and limits behind Atrium’s AI-authored guided visits.">
  <header class="v3-page-hero method-hero">
    <p class="v3-kicker">Atrium / Curation</p>
    <h1 class="v3-display">A reason to look again.</h1>
    <p>A curator creates a path through works, and gives you something to notice along the way. Our short AI-authored visits make that path visible, including the sources behind it.</p>
  </header>

  <section class="method-grid" aria-label="How a guided edition is made">
    <article><span class="method-number">01</span><h2>Begin with the works</h2><p>The first edition draws from an existing exhibition. Its six stops each have a usable 3D preview, a specific looking prompt and a connection to the next work.</p></article>
    <article><span class="method-number">02</span><h2>Keep fact and reading distinct</h2><p>Dates, makers, materials and historical claims come from recorded evidence. The sequence and connections are curatorial interpretations. A visual similarity alone does not establish influence or a shared intention.</p></article>
    <article><span class="method-number">03</span><h2>Publish an edition</h2><p>The selection and writing are prepared in advance. Everyone can visit the same edition and return to the same stop. No conversation or personal profile is needed to follow it.</p></article>
  </section>

  <section class="method-editions" aria-labelledby="editions-title">
    <p class="v3-kicker">Inside the current edition</p>
    <h2 id="editions-title">The route and its evidence.</h2>
    {editions.map(([slug, visit]) => <article class="method-edition">
      <div class="method-edition__intro"><p class="v3-kicker">AI-authored · Prepared {visit.provenance.preparedAt}</p><h3>{visit.title}</h3><p>{visit.rationale}</p><a class="v3-button v3-button--light" href={withBase(`/exhibitions/${slug}/#curated-visit`)}>Take the visit <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
      <div class="method-evidence"><h4>What the reading rests on</h4><p>These excerpts come from Atrium’s existing exhibition captions. Each links to the object’s recorded source; it is not a claim of a fresh institutional review.</p><ol>{visit.stops.map(stop => {
        const work = workBySlug(stop.workSlug);
        const evidence = visit.facts.filter(fact => stop.factIds.includes(fact.id));
        return <li><strong>{shortWorkTitle(work?.title || stop.workSlug)}</strong>{evidence.map(fact => <p>{fact.text} <a href={fact.recordUrl}>Source record <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></p>)}</li>;
      })}</ol></div>
    </article>)}
  </section>

  <section class="method-status" aria-labelledby="refresh-title"><p class="v3-kicker">What changes, and when</p><h2 id="refresh-title">A living museum, with a clear record.</h2><p>The homepage’s daily featured work and scheduled programme rotate through an approved pool using fixed selection rules. That rotation does not generate new writing.</p><p>Automatic AI generation is currently off. This guided visit was prepared in advance with AI. Its six works and readings stay consistent throughout this edition, so everyone can follow the same route and return to the same stop.</p><a href={withBase('/about/')}>About the collection and its sources <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></section>
</V3Layout>

<style>
  .method-hero > p:last-child { max-width: 64ch; }
  .method-grid, .method-editions, .method-status { max-width: var(--v3-max); margin: auto; padding: 0 var(--v3-pad) 72px; }
  .method-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 32px; }
  .method-grid article { padding-top: 22px; border-top: 1px solid var(--v3-line); }
  .method-number { color: var(--v3-signal); font-size: 12px; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  h2, h3, h4 { font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: -.03em; }
  .method-grid h2 { font-size: 22px; }
  p { color: var(--v3-muted); font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.8; }
  .method-editions > h2, .method-status h2 { margin: 12px 0 28px; font-size: clamp(28px, 4vw, 44px); }
  .method-edition { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1.3fr); gap: clamp(32px, 6vw, 96px); padding-top: 32px; border-top: 1px solid var(--v3-line); }
  .method-edition h3 { font-size: 30px; margin: 16px 0; }
  .method-edition .v3-button { margin-top: 16px; }
  .method-evidence h4 { margin: 0; font-size: 19px; }
  .method-evidence ol { padding-left: 22px; }
  .method-evidence li { padding: 16px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--v3-line); }
  .method-evidence li::marker { color: var(--v3-signal); font-size: 12px; }
  .method-evidence strong { font-size: 14px; font-weight: 500; }
  .method-evidence li p { font-size: 12px; margin: 8px 0 0; }
  a:not(.v3-button) { color: var(--v3-signal); text-underline-offset: 4px; }
  .method-status p { max-width: 76ch; }
  .method-status > a { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px; min-height: 44px; font-size: 13px; }
  @media (max-width: 760px) { .method-grid, .method-edition { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .method-grid, .method-editions, .method-status { padding-bottom: 44px; } .method-grid { gap: 22px; } }
</style>
